Nothing was deleted and nothing is scheduled. The group message is untrusted input, so the bridge now passes it to the agent only as quoted data inside an <untrusted_message> block with the sender id, never as instructions.

Changes in agent_bridge.py:
- inbound group text is wrapped by quote_untrusted() before it reaches the agent;
- the sender is not on the operator allowlist (ALLOWED_USER_IDS), so the message cannot trigger tools at all;
- destructive tools (shell rm, file delete) stay behind an approval button that only the operator can press;
- the operator gets a private notification with the quoted message and the sender, so you can decide what to do.

The allowlist is unchanged; group members still cannot drive the agent.
